// pseudo-code for bluetooth_device_info.dart assembly

// Class: FeatureSupport
// Purpose: A structural model used to track the presence of specific hardware capabilities 
// on a connected Bluetooth device, parsed directly from command payloads.
// Fields (Boolean Flags):
// - Bitmask-based properties for features like pairing status, audio path availability, 
//   and various sensor/hardware flags.

// Factory: FeatureSupport.fromCommand(dynamic command)
// Logic: Parses a raw byte array or primitive value containing bit-packed feature flags.
// 1. Extracts the payload from the incoming [command].
// 2. Performs bitwise masking (e.g., & 0x80, & 0x40, & 0x20) against specific offsets in the byte stream.
// 3. Maps each masked result to corresponding Boolean fields within a new FeatureSupport instance.
// 4. Specifically handles features like:
//    - Connection type/stability indicators.
//    - Presence of audio/camera integration readiness.
//    - Protocol-specific extensions retrieved from the device.

// Class: BleDeviceModel 
// Purpose: Represents a discovered Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) device, managing connection state and metadata.
// Fields (Reactive):
// - Uses GetX (`Rx`) types for reactive property tracking (e.g., `RxInt`, `RxString`).
// - Maintains properties like connection status, battery level, and signal strength.

// Function: _clearData()
// Logic: Resets the device model to a neutral "disconnected" or "uninitialized" state.
// 1. Sets all reactive identity fields (name, address) to null/empty.
// 
// 2. Resets connection-related metrics (battery index, signal strength value, etc.) to default values.
// 3. Notifies observers that the device state has been scrubbed.

// Function: _BleDeviceModel() [Constructor]
// Logic: Initializes a new BleDeviceModel with default "disconnected" values.
// 1. Sets status flags (e.s., isPairing, isHeadphone) to 'false'.
// 2. Initializes reactive integers (e.g., battery level = 0 or 255 for unknown).
// 3. Sets the identifier/name string to empty ("").
// 4. Prepares the model for incoming data updates from Scans/Connections.

// Class: MusicSharerStatus & CameraStatus (Enums)
// Purpose: High-level application state enums used to drive UI logic related to 
// simultaneous'audio sharing or camera availability features during a connection.

// Summary of file: bluetooth_device_info.dart
// This module acts as the "Truth Source" for the device-side capabilities. 
// It transforms raw, bitwise hardware responses into rich, reactive Dart objects 
// that can be used by the UI and the core Bluetooth managers to drive user interaction.
